UID:25a08609a2015bb4541a83bec2ec@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Praised for her “fearless virtuosity\,” and “capacity fo
 r pure theatre and drama”\, Laura Lootens has emerged as one of the most
  compelling classical guitarists of her generation – from a concert debu
 t at the prestigious Amsterdam Concertgebouw to recognition as a Classic F
 M Rising Star. This season\, she brings her Dreams & Caprices to stages ac
 ross the United States. In this recital\, music by Chopin\, Mertz\, and Ba
 rrios meets the striking modernism of George Rochberg\, moving from Romant
 ic elegies and waltzes to intricate\, virtuosic caprices. The guitar shift
 s from whispered intimacy to breathtaking virtuosity\, opening up an entir
 e world of colour and emotion. Join us for an evening of exceptio\nCategor
 y: Music\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/laura-lootens-dr
 eams-and-caprices/
LOCATION:Emory Performing Arts Studio\, 1804 N Decatur Rd\, Atlanta\, GA\,
  30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/laura-lootens-dreams-and-caprices/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
