UID:5648d78defaceb792740c5f232b2@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Between Here & Infinity: Celebrating 30 Years of the Spelman C
 ollege Art Collection\, an expansive exhibition featuring nearly seventy w
 orks by Black women artists who shape our permanent collection and define 
 our mission. Beginning September 9\, 2026\, visitors to the Spelman Colleg
 e Museum will have opportunities to discover art and artists from the coll
 ection. The first exhibition to span both the museum’s galleries\, this 
 exhibition will open in two waves: at the Bank of America Gallery at the M
 ary Schmidt Campbell Center for Innovation & the Arts\, opening September 
 9\, 2026\, and in the gallery in the Camille Olivia Hanks Cosby\, Ed.D. Ac
 ademic Center on October 2\, 2026. Between Here & Infinit\nCategory: Art +
  Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/between-here-infi
 nity-celebrating-30-years-of-the-spelman-college-art-collection/2026-11-04
 /
LOCATION:Spelman College Museum of Fine Art\, 350 Spelman Ln SW\, Atlanta
 \, 30314
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/between-here-infinity-celebrating-30-yea
 rs-of-the-spelman-college-art-collection/2026-11-04/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elders Sacred Talk Series with the Congo Square Preservation Socie
 ty: Benny Jones and Zohar Israel — New Orleans
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-06:00":20261104T173000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-06:00":20261104T191500
DTSTAMP:20261030T222453Z
UID:dec0ce78e3957592290268a45fd4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Talks &amp\; Tours\,New Orleans\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In 2023\, NOMA and the Congo Square Preservation Society began
  collaborating on the Elders Sacred Talk Series\, programs that celebrate 
 the lives of prolific elder New Orleanians and provide visitors the opport
 unity to learn firsthand about the impact they’ve had on the city. The E
 lders Sacred Talk Series complements the museum’s art making workshops a
 nd underscores the important role of storytelling in New Orleans. For this
  Elders Sacred Talk program\, join Benny Jones and Zohar Israel for a conv
 ersation\, as well as a celebration honoring Big Chief “Al” & Big Quee
 n Wanda Womble of the Cheyenne Hunters Mardi Gras Indian tribe. This progr
 am is free with museum admission. No registration required\nCategory: Talk
 s &amp\; Tours\nOriginal listing: https://noma.org/event/elders-sacred-tal
 k-series-with-the-congo-square-preservation-society-benny-jones-and-zohar-
 israel/
LOCATION:New Orleans Museum of Art\, 1 Collins Diboll Cir\, New Orleans\, 
 LA 70124
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://noma.org/event/elders-sacred-talk-series-with-the-congo-square
 -preservation-society-benny-jones-and-zohar-israel/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:noma
END:VEVENT
