BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ami Taf Ra & Kamasi Washington presenting The Prophet & The Madman
  — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T193000
DTSTAMP:20261030T222453Z
UID:6b2f5e9c52ed7a9db2aa212d3455@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:City Winery Atlanta and WLCK 91.9 presents Ami Taf Ra & Kamasi
  Washington live on November 18th at 6pm and 9:30pm! Some collaborations f
 eel inevitable in hindsight. Ami Taf Ra and Kamasi Washington’s is one o
 f them. This November\, the North African\, Los Angeles based vocalist and
  composer joins Grammy winning saxophonist and producer Kamasi Washington 
 for a rare live presentation of Ami’s debut album\, The Prophet and the 
 Madman\, a project Washington produced and released through Brainfeeder. T
 he record itself defies easy categorization\, and that’s the point. Moro
 ccan Gnawa rhythms meet Arabic musical tradition\, gospel\, soul\, and spi
 ritual jazz\, all in service of a meditation on duality\, heal\nCategory: 
 Music\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/ami-taf-ra-kamasi-w
 ashington-presenting-the-prophet-the-madman/
LOCATION:City Winery Atlanta\, 650 North Ave NE\, Atlanta\, 30308
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/ami-taf-ra-kamasi-washington-presenting-
 the-prophet-the-madman/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Emory Cinematheque Presents: BAMBOOZLED (2000) — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261118T220000
DTSTAMP:20261030T222453Z
UID:66ce69ad2e90d12caadd00aa1169@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Introduced by Dr. Alessandra Raengo (Georgia State University)
  On a budget of ten million dollars and shot primarily on Mini-DV\, Spike 
 Lee wrote and directed the script for this funny and parodic examination o
 f television targeting Black audiences. Lee wanted to experiment with the 
 new technology and tapped Ellen Kuras to serve as the film’s DP (Kuras a
 lso shot 4 LITTLE GIRLS and SUMMER OF SAM). He notes\, “…digital video
  was a good aesthetic choice because it’s a film about a television show
 …using Mini-DV suited this film perfectly because we had a lot to do on 
 this shoot and we needed to move” (THE ST. LOUIS AMERICAN). Released in 
 2000\, BAMBOOZLED garnered a split reception of its meaning\, \nCategory: 
 Film + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinem
 atheque-presents-bamboozled-2000/
LOCATION:White Hall 208\, 301 Dowman Dr.\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-emory-cinematheque-presents-bamboozl
 ed-2000/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
