UID:225a42bfa0fd24882734f506c4c0@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Bad Plus are the ultimate originals. A democratic unit wit
 h a clear vision and a refusal to conform to convention. For the past two 
 decades they have played with spirit and adventure\, made their own rules 
 and done so with a bold sense of creativity and intent. Avoiding easy cate
 gorization\, The Bad Plus has won critical acclaim and a legion of fans wo
 rldwide with their unique sound and flair for live performance. The Bad Pl
 us continues to push boundaries as founding members Reid Anderson (bass) a
 nd Dave King (drums) embark on a new piano-less incarnation of the band wi
 th Ben Monder (guitar) and Chris Speed (tenor saxophone) – instigating a
  new wave of excitement and anticipation within th\nCategory: Music\nOrigi
 nal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-bad-plus-farewell-tour/
LOCATION:The Garden Club at Wild Heaven West End\, 1010 White St SW\, Atla
 nta\, GA\, 30310
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-bad-plus-farewell-tour/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TRAD — Hannah Mitchell (Atlanta Premiere) — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261120T203000
DTSTAMP:20261030T222453Z
UID:d88b37252bcc19bff1bbf47134c4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Theater\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:TRAD is a theatrical tear-down of the modern “trad wife” p
 henomenon and the Christian nationalist beliefs behind it\, which also ind
 ulges our collective yearning for fantasies of escape. This trad wife is e
 ternally pregnant and endlessly devout: what could shake the ripeness of h
 er faith? Staged as a seminar for women curious about the tradwife life\, 
 with the audience cast as the attendees. Expect to be called on. Written a
 nd performed by Hannah Mitchell. Directed by Iris McCloughan. Initially co
 -directed and devised with Meaghan Robichaud. Produced by Celebration Barn
 . Premiered to sold-out houses at The Exponential Festival (NYC) in Januar
 y 2026\; Philadelphia Fringe\, September 2026. Atlanta\nCategory: Theater
 \nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/trad-hannah-mitchell-atl
 anta-premiere/
LOCATION:React Theatre (formerly Dynamic El Dorado)\, 572 Edgewood Ave SE
 \, Suite 116\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30312
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/trad-hannah-mitchell-atlanta-premiere/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
